We also need to add a function `reset()` that sets:

- player = { x: CANVAS_WIDTH / 2, y: CANVAS_HEIGHT - 50, lane: 1 };
- hazards = [];
- score = 0;
- phase = "playing"? Or "menu"? The contract says state starts with "menu". At start page loads we may have a menu (phase "menu") but soon we can start playing; we might include `reset()` sets phase = "playing" and starts loop. For now we can set phase = "playing". There's also a concept of "player" being visible. We'll set state accordingly.

- Set `lastTime = performance.now();`.

- call `startLoop()`;

- In page load initially we need to call reset or start loop? The instruction for Task 4 only mentions input handling resetting; but we may need to start game loop after reset is called perhaps on load. For now we will call reset() at end of script after definitions to start game. Or we may call reset() at end of script similar to reference; but that may be later tasks. The page must load cleanly and not error. Starting a loop will call update (which does nothing) and render (which does nothing), but that's fine. However we might need to ensure we have a canvas context etc.

We might call reset() at page load after establishing input listeners.

Implementation steps:

- Add functions for `reset()`.

- Add event listeners:

```js
document.addEventListener("keydown", (ev) => {
  if (ev.key === "r" || ev.key === "R") { reset(); return; }
  if (ev.key === "ArrowLeft" || ev.key === "a" || ev.key === "A") { keys.add("left"); }
  if (ev.key === "ArrowRight" || ev.key === "d" || ev.key === "D") { keys.add("right"); }
});
document.addEventListener("keyup", (ev) => {
  if (ev.key === "ArrowLeft" || ev.key === "a" || ev.key === "A") { keys.delete("left"); }
  if (ev.key === "ArrowRight" || ev.key === "d" || ev.key === "D") { keys.delete("right"); }
});
restartBtn.addEventListener("click", reset);
```

- Also set up "keys" to hold pressed keys, later used.

